cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'PEAC: Verifiable Interaction Records for Machine-to-Machine Systems'
message: 'If you use PEAC, please cite this repository.'
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Raj
    given-names: Jithin
    email: contact@peacprotocol.org
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0009-7602-1629'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/peacprotocol/peac'
url: 'https://www.peacprotocol.org'
abstract: >-
  PEAC is an open protocol for portable, verifiable interaction records across
  agent, tool, API, and cross-runtime workflows. Records are signed JWS
  artifacts (Interaction Record Format 0.2) with deterministic verification
  semantics, so independent implementations produce the same accept or reject
  decision.
keywords:
  - interaction-records
  - signed-records
  - offline-verification
  - jws
  - ed25519
  - mcp
  - agents
  - evidence
license: Apache-2.0
version: '0.16.4'
date-released: '2026-08-09'
